From d04f4516cf720bf8ff72a5626cf176da047aa9f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Dutta, Ranjan" <ranjan.dutta@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:41:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] media: i2c: imx390: drop local MAX() definition

v6.6.158 picked up upstream commit 6183c6579356 ("minmax: make generic
MIN() and MAX() macros available everywhere"), which defines MAX() in
<linux/minmax.h>. imx390.c gets that header through <linux/acpi.h>, so
its own MAX() now redefines it and breaks the build with CONFIG_WERROR:

  drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c:69: error: "MAX" redefined [-Werror]

Drop the local definition and use the generic one, as upstream did for
the other in-tree users. The semantics are identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c
index c81e46c22c880..8e3eb41772bf3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx390.c
@@ -66,8 +66,6 @@
 #define IMX390_BLUE_BALANCE_STEP	1
 #define IMX390_BLUE_BALANCE_DEF		0x100
 
-#define MAX(a, b)		(((a) > (b)) ? (a) : (b))
-
 #define IMX390_CID_CSI_PORT         (V4L2_CID_USER_BASE | 0x1001)
 #define IMX390_CID_I2C_BUS         (V4L2_CID_USER_BASE | 0x1002)
 #define IMX390_CID_I2C_ID         (V4L2_CID_USER_BASE | 0x1003)
-- 
2.43.0

